{"chunk_id": "018b111bbdbc", "text": "This chapter narrates the climactic duel between Lakshmana (Saumitri) and Ravana\u2019s formidable son Indrajita during the war in Lanka. After his first chariot is destroyed, Indrajita briefly retreats, returns in a new chariot, and unleashes a devastating assault that scatters the monkey army. Lakshmana, aided by Vibhishana, counters with extraordinary archery, shattering Indrajita\u2019s weapons, killing his charioteer, and forcing him to fight on foot. The battle escalates into a mythic exchange of divine missiles\u2014those of Yama, Varuna, Rudra, Agni, and others\u2014while celestial beings watch from the sky. At last Lakshmana invokes Indra\u2019s irresistible weapon, vowing that if Rama is truly righteous it will strike true. The arrow severs Indrajita\u2019s head, turning the tide of the war and triggering the rout of the demon army.\nLakshmana and Indrajita engage in a fierce duel of celestial weapons, ending when Lakshmana invokes Indra\u2019s weapon and beheads Ravana\u2019s son.\nThemes: heroic duel, divine weapons, fate and destiny, loyalty to Rama, fall of a champion", "vector": [-0.0005836963537149131, -0.010393993929028511, 0.0013353627873584628, 0.01091806124895811, -0.007551938761025667, 0.013672771863639355, -0.02468489669263363, -0.014982938766479492, -0.024725208058953285, -0.02057298645377159, 0.023273946717381477, 0.015977323055267334, 0.013276361860334873, 0.0027832656633108854, 0.005600125528872013, 0.011193531565368176, 0.03872720152139664, -0.024993961676955223, 0.029293997213244438, -0.01220135297626257, -0.014714187011122704, -0.01007149089127779, -0.007155529223382473, 0.020586423575878143, -0.021768933162093163, 0.004881212953478098, 0.014042305760085583, -0.030127128586173058, 0.02055954933166504, -0.0063929446041584015, -0.010259618051350117, -0.019820479676127434, 0.008042411878705025, -0.010414150543510914, -0.02182268351316452, -0.013444332405924797, 0.0021130647510290146, -0.0110524371266365